AB  - This paper proposes a change detection model based on Gaussian pyramids and deep convolutional neural networks. The model introduces the multi-scale representation of the image in the Gaussian pyramid, improves the difference between the changed samples and the unchanged samples in the data set, and studies the DAF process for evaluating the performance of phosphorus removal in the watershed. The results show that the compound coagulant PAM-PAC/ The PFS phosphorus removal system has a good phosphorus removal effect on the production sewage of the phosphate mining enterprises in the east tributary of Huangbai River, and has a great reduction effect on the effluent turbidity. The relationship between degrees (x, NTU) satisfies $\mathrm{y}=0.0363\mathrm{x}+0.0747 (\mathrm{R}2=0.9013)$.
