AB  - In this paper, a weakly-supervised change detection model (Siam-DenNet) is proposed, the model requires only image-level labels for end-to-end training. The feature extraction network of this model is a pair of Siamese networks that share parameters, each branch uses the DenseNet network for feature extraction, in order to fully combine the feature of the lower and upper levels, all the feature diagrams generated by DenseBlock are cascaded. Since the pixels changed in the image are much smaller than the unchanged pixels, which leads to the problem of positive and negative samples and difficult sample imbalance, Hard negative mining method is adopted and the Focal Loss function is introduced. Finally, CRF is used to constrain the boundaries of the split object to ensure that the variation segmentation diagram is more accurate. This paper shows the segmentation and classification performance of the proposed model, and obtains advanced results on two public data sets, AICD and HRSCD.
