AB  - Smart agricultural tourism information system based on the data mining and rural revitalization estimation through remote sensing images is studied in the paper. When the pure coherent wave emitted by the imaging radar irradiates the target, the scattered signal of the random scattering surface on the target will interfere with the emitted coherent signal, resulting in coherent speckle noise in the image, hence, the image modification model is considered. Through the comprehensive evaluation of the classification results, it is proved that the farmland extraction method takes into account the advantages of pixel-level classification and object-level segmentation, effectively avoids the salt and pepper effect, inaccurate boundaries of land object classification and other disadvantages of the traditional classification methods, and improves the classification of the farmland precision. Furthermore, the application on the SATIS is discussed and verified to show the robustness of the model.
