AB  - The growing demand for efficient mapping and monitoring of a wide variety of sites, encouraged by the democratization of uncrewed aerial system (UAS) based solutions using standard commercial hyperspectral cameras, calls for an integrated remote sensing approach such that the end-to-end raw-to-reflectance data processing can be done at the desired timescales by the average end user. The m4mining project aims to further synergize UAS and satellite-based processing routines for operational use at mining sites. For that purpose, an automated hyperspectral imaging (HSI) data processor from raw data acquisition to geocoded products was developed. The processor is designed for a high-precision workflow, including full atmospheric correction and reflectance retrieval on the basis of hyperspectral point cloud data representation. Using pre-recorded test data, we show that the processor can produce high quality results in under three hours for 100 GB of data acquisition.
