PY  - 2025
PB  - IEEE
DO  - 10.1109/CAC67268.2025.11486684
SN  - 2688-0938
AB  - Ground fissures in coal mine goafs critically undermine ecological stability and production safety. Addressing the inefficiency of conventional monitoring, this paper proposes GF-SegNext for precise fissure identification in UAV imagery. The network integrates a Dilated Residual Network (MSCAN) extracting multi-scale geological contexts, an HFP attention mechanism enhancing boundary features, a Spatial-Local Attention Module (GLB) capturing morphological details in complex backgrounds, and Efficient Multi-scale Channel Attention (EMA) fusing feature dependencies. Evaluated on a dedicated GF dataset, GF-SegNext achieves 63.18% Recall, 74.95% MIoU and 83.4% MDice, demonstrating significant improvements in high-risk zone identification. Cross-validation on the DeepCrack dataset confirms its generalization capability for fissure recognition. This study delivers a reliable technical solution for intelligent geological hazard monitoring in mining areas.
