AB  - The primary purpose of remote sensing interpretation is to acquire information on geological elements in the study area by collecting geological data and comparing remote sensing images [1]. This study employs Synthetic Aperture Radar Interferometry (InSAR) technology to monitor ground deformation around the Lao Cai area in Vietnam. Using 26 Sentinel-1 SAR images, we detected surface deformation occurring between October 2020 and August 2021, generating a regional InSAR deformation map. The results provide insights into post-mining surface deformation patterns, enable monitoring of mining-induced subsidence, assess geological environmental damage, and support early warning systems for geohazards.
