AB  - The distribution and diffusion of mining tailings, charged with toxic minerals, throughout mining areas are an important issue because abandoned tailings can be a major source of environmental pollution. Characterization is the first step for the inventory and efficient monitoring of the abundance of minerals with high pollution potential in a quick and timely fashion is crucial for protecting the natural environment, within soils around Hammam Zriba mine in Northen Tunisia. In this study, we propose an approach based on VNIR-SWIR field Hyperspectral spectroscopy with respect to XRD laboratory analysis. Particularly, detecting changes of mineral concentrations that were measured in the same collection points at different time series is of special interest in this application domain.
