AB  - Illegal logging, unregulated mining, and improper waste disposal continue to pose significant threats to global ecosystems. Monitoring these activities in real time is challenging due to the large geographic areas involved and the fragmented nature of available data. To address this, we developed EcoProfiler, an open source intelligence (OSINT) framework that consolidates diverse environmental data sources. The system integrates geospatial information from Google Earth Engine and Sentinel-2 satellite imagery with contextual insights from corporate registries such as OpenSanctions, social media platforms including Reddit, and global news feeds via NewsAPI. EcoProfiler provides a command-line interface for automated data acquisition and a Streamlit dashboard for interactive visualization, including maps and network graphs. Additionally, a composite risk scoring mechanism prioritizes areas based on satellite alert density and flagged entities, supporting efficient decision-making by investigators. Evaluation results demonstrate a 92% accuracy in entity extraction and a reduction of manual research time by 40%. Overall, EcoProfiler offers a scalable and systematic approach to transforming dispersed environmental data into actionable intelligence for enforcement agencies and policymakers.
