AB  - Mineral resource exploitation represents an important sector of the economy of the Republic of Moldova; however, extractive activities may generate significant environmental impacts, including terrain modification, soil degradation, and disturbance of local ecosystems. In this context, the use of technologies based on Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) provides a modern and efficient method for monitoring mining activities and assessing the ecological restoration processes of affected land areas. This paper analyzes the application of UAV-based technologies integrated with digital photogrammetry and LiDAR scanning methods for generating three-dimensional models, orthophotoplans, and Digital Elevation Models (DEM) used for the analysis of morphological changes in mining sites. By processing the collected data in specialized software such as Agisoft Metashape and CloudCompare, precise assessments of excavated volumes, slope stability monitoring, and analysis of land rehabilitation processes can be performed. The obtained results demonstrate that the use of UAV technology significantly improves the efficiency of monitoring mineral exploitation activities, contributes to better natural resource management, and supports ecological restoration processes in areas affected by extractive activities in the Republic of Moldova.
