AB  - Remote sensing image change detection is vital for monitoring environmental evolution and disaster response. However, multitemporal images often suffer from resolution mismatches due to sensor differences and observation conditions, reducing detection accuracy. Existing methods relying on downsampling or interpolation lose semantic features. To address this, we propose SRDN, a change detection model combining diffusion models with super-resolution. First, a super-resolution module enhances low-resolution images with a content loss to reduce information loss. Then, a diffusion model integrates multi-resolution features to capture global and local information. Finally, an Atrous Spatial Pyramid Pooling with Efficient Multi-scale Attention forms a change perception module (FCPB) for multi-scale feature fusion and temporal difference mining. Experiments on WHU-CD and CDD datasets show that SRDN achieves superior performance under 4× and 8× resolution differences compared with existing methods.
