AB  - Multi-scale visual representation have shown their advantages in effectiveness in a wide range of applications. However, existing methods fail to fully utilize the specific semantic information of the respective layers, as they focus too much on the interaction between different scale layers. To alleviate this problem, in this paper, we propose a new framework inspired by YOLO efficiency, which injects the unique information of the respective layers for cross-scale communication. Specifically, we first propose the Mining Unique Semantics module (MUS), which explicitly enhances the unique contextual semantics in each layer. Second, although it is crucial to leverage global context-enhanced features from other layers, overemphasis may inadvertently ignore the intrinsic semantic information within each layer. To this end, we design a Multi-Scale Information Integration module (MSI) that carefully balances this trade-off, ensuring meaningful integration without sacrificing individual identity. With the help of the above two modules, our proposed method effectively leverages small-scale object features related to spatial positions to improve detection performance in Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAV) object detection tasks. Extensive experiments on the VisDrone2019 benchmark dataset show that the proposed framework achieves superior performance compared with advanced UAV object detection methods.
